---
layout: none
---
[
  {%- comment -%}
  Excerpt only. This previously indexed each page's ENTIRE rendered text, which
  made the file 10.3 MB - 99.6% of it content, with a single entry (the
  tryhackme index) holding 6.9 MB on its own. Browsers fetch this on first
  search, so it was the slowest thing on the site by a wide margin.

  Truncating to 400 characters of stripped text takes the file to roughly
  280 KB. Search still matches on title and opening text, which is what people
  actually search for. Do not restore the full content without also splitting
  the index per platform.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% assign pages = site.pages | where_exp: "p", "p.title" %}
  {% for post in pages %}
    {
      "title": "{{ post.title | escape }}",
      "url": "{{ post.url | relative_url }}",
      "content": {{ post.content | strip_html | strip_newlines | strip | truncate: 400 | jsonify }}
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
]